      "text": "To determine the fraction of the items on the menu that I can eat, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of dishes on the menu:**\n   Let \\( T \\) be the total number of dishes on the menu. We know that one fifth of the menu is vegetarian dishes. Therefore, the number of vegetarian dishes is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{T}{5}\n   \\]\n   We are given that there are 4 vegetarian dishes. So, we can write:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{T}{5} = 4\n   \\]\n   To find \\( T \\), we multiply both sides of the equation by 5:\n   \\[\n   T = 4 \\times 5 = 20\n   \\]\n   So, the total number of dishes on the menu is 20.\n\n2. **Determine the number of gluten-free vegetarian dishes:**\n   We know that 4 out of the 20 dishes are vegetarian, and 3 of these vegetarian dishes contain gluten. Therefore, the number of vegetarian gluten-free dishes is:\n   \\[\n   4 - 3 = 1\n   \\]\n   So, there is 1 vegetarian gluten-free dish on the menu.\n\n3. **Calculate the fraction of the menu that I can eat:**\n   The fraction of the menu that I can eat is the number of vegetarian gluten-free dishes divided by the total number of dishes on the menu:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{20}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the fraction of the items on the menu that I can eat is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{20}}\\).",
