      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the fraction of the items on the menu that I can eat, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of dishes without meat:**\n   The problem states that there are four dishes without meat in total.\n\n2. **Determine the number of meatless dishes that contain gluten:**\n   It is given that three of the four meatless dishes contain gluten.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of meatless dishes that do not contain gluten:**\n   Since there are four meatless dishes in total and three of them contain gluten, the number of meatless dishes that do not contain gluten is:\n   \\[\n   4 - 3 = 1\n   \\]\n   So, there is only one meatless dish that does not contain gluten.\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of dishes on the menu:**\n   We know that the four meatless dishes without gluten represent one fifth of the total menu. Let \\( T \\) be the total number of dishes on the menu. Then:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{5}T = 4\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( T \\):\n   \\[\n   T = 4 \\times 5 = 20\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the total number of dishes on the menu is 20.\n\n5. **Determine the number of dishes I can eat:**\n   I can eat all the dishes that do not contain gluten, which are the four meatless dishes without gluten and the one meatless dish that does not contain gluten. Thus, the total number of dishes I can eat is:\n   \\[\n   4 + 1 = 5\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the fraction of the total menu that I can eat:**\n   The fraction of the total menu that I can eat is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{5}{20} = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the fraction of the items on the menu at the restaurant that I can eat is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\).",
